# GitHub Pull Request #76

## Title
fix: stop a pi-action run that the agent starts inside a run

## Description
"Follow-up to #66 ([comment](https://github.com/cv/pi-action/issues/66#issuecomment-6866884832)).\n\n## What happened\n\nIn [run 43520110827](https://github.com/cv/pi-action/actions/runs/43520110827/job/132211946823), the agent ran `node src/index.ts` (from pit's `shell.execFile`) as a smoke test. The child had the step's environment: the event, the `INPUT_*` values, and the tokens. So it ran the action again on issue #66 in the same checkout. It committed to `refs/pi-action/threads/66` under the outer run, whose `GitStorage` then failed its compare-and-swap (`Ref refs/pi-action/threads/66 moved`), and the run failed.\n\n## Change\n\n- New `src/nested-run.ts`: `claimRun(env)` sets `PI_ACTION_RUNNING=<pid>` in pi-action's own `process.env`. Every tool and child process inherits it: `bash`, and also pit, which runs in the pi-action process and spawns from its environment.\n- `src/index.ts` calls it first. When the variable is already set, the step fails at once (`setFailed`), before it reads the inputs or touches a ref.\n- `src/push.ts` (the `Save pi thread state` step) pushes nothing inside a run, with a warning. The real push step is a new process without the variable, so it still works.\n- Docs: \"A run inside a run\" in `docs/security.md`, and the new file in CONTRIBUTING's source table.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `claimRun` / `nestedRun`: marks, refuses with the outer run's mark kept, ignores an empty value.\n- `node src/index.ts` and `node src/push.ts` under plain Node with the variable set: exit 1 with the error, and exit 0 with the warning. The children get only `PATH` and the variable, so if the guard broke, they would find no event or token to act on.\n\n`npm run check` passes.\n\n## Release note\n\n```markdown\n### Fixed\n- **A run that the agent starts inside a run stops at once** (#76). If the agent ran pi-action again from its tools, the second run changed the thread refs under the first, and the first run failed. pi-action now sets `PI_ACTION_RUNNING` while it runs and does not start when it is set. See [A run inside a run](https://github.com/cv/pi-action/blob/vX.Y.Z/docs/security.md#a-run-inside-a-run).\n```"


## Task
fix PR description, and let's figure out how to stop this bad formatting from happening

## Your Reply

pi-action posts your final response as a comment on this issue or pull request. **Do not post your reply yourself**, for example with `gh issue comment`, `gh pr comment`, `gh pr review`, or `gh api`. That would post the same answer twice. Use `gh` to comment only where the task asks for it, such as on another issue.

## Important: Artifact and Script Requirements

**CRITICAL:** After the GitHub Action finishes running, all files modified or created are lost, and the GitHub Action runner is destroyed. Therefore:

1. **All generated code and artifacts MUST be committed** - Any files you create, modify, or generate must be committed and pushed to the repository before the action completes. Nothing will persist otherwise.

2. **Any throw-away scripts generated MUST be run immediately** - If you create temporary scripts (like `/tmp/create-issues.sh` or similar), you must execute them during the same session. They will be lost when the runner terminates.

3. **Commit and push all work** - Always end your work by committing and pushing changes to ensure they persist beyond the GitHub Action execution.

